system "Shared counter with a lock"

# The fix for examples/broken/lost-update.zin: a worker must hold the lock
# from its read to its write.

types
  worker is one of alice, bob
  phase is one of idle, holding, done

state
  counter is an integer from 0 to 2
  seen is a map from worker to an integer from 0 to 2
  at is a map from worker to phase
  locked is a boolean

initially
  counter is 0
  seen of every worker is 0
  at of every worker is idle
  locked is false

always
  counter is number of w in worker where at of w is done
  locked is some w in worker satisfies at of w is holding

eventually
  counter is 2

terminal when every w in worker satisfies at of w is done

action read(w is a worker)
  requires at of w is idle
  requires not locked
  locked becomes true
  seen of w becomes counter
  at of w becomes holding

action write(w is a worker)
  requires at of w is holding
  counter becomes seen of w + 1
  at of w becomes done
  locked becomes false

scenario "One after the other"
  read(alice)
  reject read(bob)
  write(alice)
  read(bob)
  write(bob)
  expect counter is 2
